{"eligibility":"exclude","exclusion_criterion":"IC3","side_list":"correctness-only","eligibility_reason":"The paper fine-tunes ControlledCoder via rejection-sampling SFT, but its only outcomes are correctness pass@1 and instruction-constraint compliance pass@1. The constraints (e.g., palindrome variable names, Greek lambda parameters, line limits, mandatory recursion) are arbitrary format adherence checks, not a measure of readability, efficiency or security quality.","title":"IFEvalCode: Controlled Code Generation","year":2025,"venue":"preprint","venue_type":"","study_type":"","techniques":"","compute_reported":"","contamination_handled":"","human_eval":"","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"","reimplementable":"","qa":"","confidence":"low","notes":"Borderline exclusion. Some constraints touch style, naming and complexity, but they are reported only as one aggregate instruction-following pass rate, with no breakdown by NF dimension. The ablation (Table 5) reports Instr.avg rising from 20.7 to 34.2. A reviewer could argue for inclusion under readability-maintainability as 'style compliance'. The extracted tables are garbled."}
