{"eligibility":"include","exclusion_criterion":"","side_list":"none","eligibility_reason":"Proposes a retrieval-augmented prompting technique in which GPT-3.5 rewrites C# methods to fix performance inefficiencies. Efficiency outcomes are reported quantitatively through expert-judged equivalent-or-better fixes and match to developer fixes. Borderline: the input is human-written code, so this may be 'adjacent' (LLM repair of human code), but the LLM does generate the edited code.","title":"RAPGen: An Approach for Fixing Code Inefficiencies in Zero-Shot","year":2023,"venue":"2025 IEEE/ACM 47th International Conference on Software Engineering: Software Engineering in Practice (ICSE-SEIP)","venue_type":"peer-reviewed-conf","study_type":"technique-proposal","techniques":[{"technique_name":"RAPGen (Retrieval-Augmented Prompt Generation)","family_v0":"retrieval","stage":"pre-generation","signal_source":["retrieved-knowledge","profiler"],"tools":"Aroma code search; profiler-based bug localization (in-the-wild); heuristic diff localization for evaluation","iterations":"","dims_targeted":["efficiency"],"dims_measured":["efficiency"],"correctness_measured":false,"metrics":"efficiency: expert judgment that the fix is equivalent or better than the developer fix in performance (Closest Match Top-K, human); verbatim/abstracted match and CodeBLEU against the developer performance fix (similarity-to-reference); developer survey in the wild (human)","benchmarks":"DeepDev-PERF C# performance-fix dataset, 132 instances; in-the-wild evaluation on 10 internal .NET services","languages":"C#","models":"gpt-3.5-turbo (closed, instruct)","baselines":"Static prompt; retrieval-based one-shot prompt; reasoning-based prompt; DeepDev-PERF (fine-tuned BART)","effect_target":"+","effect_target_headline":"Closest Match Top-K Accuracy @100: 60.6 (RAPGen) vs 33.3 static prompt, 34.1 DeepDev-PERF; Verbatim Match 42.4","effect_correctness":"NR","effect_correctness_headline":"","effect_other_dims":{"readability-maintainability":"NR","efficiency":"targeted","security":"NR"}}],"compute_reported":["calls"],"contamination_handled":"no","human_eval":"rating","human_eval_details":"2 performance experts; a fix counted correct only if both agreed; no agreement statistic reported. Plus 8 developer responses in the in-the-wild evaluation.","artifact_url":"","reimplementable":"partial","qa":{"QA1":1,"QA2":1,"QA3":0.5,"QA4":0,"QA5":0,"QA6":0,"QA7":0.5,"QA8":0,"QA9":0,"QA10":1},"confidence":"low","notes":"Borderline between include and the 'adjacent' side list (LLM repair of human code). No execution-based performance measurement: the fixes could not be built or run. Efficiency was judged by experts or by match to developer fixes. Single model; 100 samples per task at temperature 0.7."}
